{{DISPLAYTITLE:Help:Saintapedia Graph}}

'''Saintapedia Graph''' turns [[mw:Extension:Cargo|Cargo]] query results into interactive [[mw:Extension:Mermaid|Mermaid]] flowcharts — especially '''organization charts''' and '''funder → fundee''' (or any source → target) networks.

{{note|This help page documents the '''MVP''' of the extension as installed on this wiki. Advanced features (styles by field, subgraphs, special-page builder, Lua) are planned for later.}}

== Requirements ==

* [[mw:Extension:Cargo|Extension:Cargo]] (required)
* Saintapedia Graph (this extension)
* MediaWiki 1.39+ / PHP 8.1+

'''You do ''not'' need Extension:Mermaid.''' Saintapedia Graph ships a bundled Mermaid library and renders diagrams itself.

== Quick start ==

=== 1. Declare Cargo tables ===

'''Organizations''' (hierarchy / org chart):

<pre>
{{#cargo_declare:_table=Organizations
|Name=String
|ParentOrg=Page
|Type=String
|Country=String
|Website=URL
}}
</pre>

'''Grants''' (edges / funding network):

<pre>
{{#cargo_declare:_table=Grants
|Funder=Page
|Recipient=Page
|Amount=Float
|Year=Integer
|Program=String
}}
</pre>

Store rows with <code>#cargo_store</code> (usually from a template), then create the tables at [[Special:CargoTables]] if needed.

=== 2. Draw an org chart ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Organizations
|fields=_pageName=Name,ParentOrg,Type
|parent_field=ParentOrg
|node_id=Name
|node_label=Name
|direction=TD
|clickable=yes
}}
</pre>

Edges are drawn '''parent → child''' (top-down reporting line).

=== 3. Draw a funding network ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Grants
|fields=Funder,Recipient,Amount,Year
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|direction=LR
|clickable=yes
|theme=forest
}}
</pre>

=== Live demo on this wiki ===

See [[Saintapedia Graph demo]] for seeded Organizations + Grants data.

== Relationship modes ==

You must choose '''one''' mode per diagram (mixing them is an error).

{| class="wikitable"
! Mode
! When to use
! Required parameters
! Edge direction
|-
| '''Hierarchy (parent)'''
| Org charts, subsidiaries, “reports to”
| <code>parent_field=…</code>
| Parent → child
|-
| '''Edge (source / target)'''
| Funding, partnerships, ownership links
| <code>source_field=…</code> '''and''' <code>target_field=…</code>
| Source → target
|}

Optional edge caption: <code>edge_label=Amount</code> (or any field).

== Parameters ==

=== Cargo query (same spirit as <code>#cargo_query</code>) ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Description
|-
| <code>tables</code> / <code>table</code>
| '''Required.''' One or more Cargo tables (comma-separated). Use table aliases if needed.
|-
| <code>fields</code>
| Columns to select. The extension will add any fields it still needs for the diagram.
|-
| <code>where</code>
| Filter (Cargo/SQL-style conditions).
|-
| <code>join on</code>
| Join conditions when using multiple tables. '''Required if more than one table.'''
|-
| <code>group by</code> / <code>having</code>
| Aggregation (same rules as Cargo).
|-
| <code>order by</code>
| Sort order.
|-
| <code>limit</code>
| Max rows (capped by site config, typically 1000).
|-
| <code>offset</code>
| Skip initial rows.
|}

=== Diagram ===

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter
! Default
! Description
|-
| <code>direction</code>
| <code>TD</code>
| Layout: <code>TD</code> (top-down), <code>LR</code> (left-right), <code>BT</code>, <code>RL</code>
|-
| <code>node_id</code>
| <code>_pageName</code>
| Field that uniquely identifies a node
|-
| <code>node_label</code>
| same as <code>node_id</code>
| Text shown on the node
|-
| <code>page_field</code>
| hierarchy: <code>_pageName</code>; edge: ends themselves
| Wiki page title used for click links
|-
| <code>parent_field</code>
| —
| Hierarchy mode only
|-
| <code>source_field</code> / <code>target_field</code>
| —
| Edge mode only (both required)
|-
| <code>edge_label</code>
| —
| Optional edge caption field
|-
| <code>link_style</code>
| <code>--></code>
| <code>--></code>, <code>-.-></code>, <code>==></code>, <code>---</code>, <code><--></code>
|-
| <code>clickable</code>
| <code>yes</code>
| <code>yes</code>/<code>no</code> — click node opens the wiki page
|-
| <code>theme</code>
| <code>default</code>
| Mermaid theme: <code>default</code>, <code>forest</code>, <code>dark</code>, <code>neutral</code>, …
|-
| <code>format</code>
| <code>mermaid</code>
| <code>mermaid</code> (render) or <code>raw</code> (source only, for debugging)
|}

'''Alias:''' <code>{{#cargo_mermaid:…}}</code> accepts the same parameters as <code>{{#saintapedia_graph:…}}</code>.

== Multiple Cargo tables ==

'''Yes — multi-table queries work''', using the same rules as <code>#cargo_query</code>:

* List every table in <code>tables=</code>
* Provide a full <code>join on=</code> chain so Cargo can connect them
* Point diagram fields at the correct table columns (aliases or <code>Table.Field</code>)

=== Example: style-ready join (edges + org type) ===

<pre>
{{#saintapedia_graph:
tables=Grants,Organizations
|join on=Grants.Funder=Organizations._pageName
|fields=Grants.Funder,Grants.Recipient,Grants.Amount,Organizations.Type
|source_field=Funder
|target_field=Recipient
|edge_label=Amount
|direction=LR
|limit=300
}}
</pre>

'''What this does today'''

* One Cargo result set → one set of nodes and edges
* In '''edge mode''', each row is one edge; node names come from source/target values
* Joins can enrich filters or edge labels (e.g. amount from Grants)

'''What multi-table does ''not'' fully do yet (MVP limits)'''

* No automatic “nodes from table A, edges from table B” dual-query mode
* No per-end styling from a second table’s Type field (planned: <code>style_by</code>)
* No recursive multi-hop expansion (“show everyone within 2 steps of X”)

For complex multi-table graphs, common patterns:

# Filter with a join, keep edge fields simple (example above)
# Pre-materialize a Cargo view table that already holds Source/Target/Label
# Use two diagrams on one page (org chart + funding network) rather than one giant graph

== Tips for good graphs ==

* Prefer '''Page'''-type fields for parent/funder/recipient so click links resolve
* Keep <code>limit=</code> reasonable (hundreds, not tens of thousands)
* Use <code>where=</code> to focus (year, type, program)
* <code>direction=TD</code> for org charts; <code>LR</code> for networks
* <code>format=raw</code> if a diagram fails — inspect Mermaid source
* Hard-refresh the browser after extension updates (Ctrl+Shift+R)

== Troubleshooting ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Symptom
! What to try
|-
| “tables parameter is required”
| Add <code>tables=YourTable</code>
|-
| Missing parent / edge fields
| Set <code>parent_field</code> '''or''' both <code>source_field</code> and <code>target_field</code> (not both modes at once)
|-
| No results
| Check Cargo data at [[Special:CargoTables]]; re-save pages that <code>#cargo_store</code>
|-
| “Diagram failed to render”
| Hard-refresh; try <code>format=raw</code>; check browser console
|-
| Too many expensive parser functions
| Fewer graphs per page, or raise <code>$wgExpensiveParserFunctionLimit</code>
|-
| Join error from Cargo
| Ensure <code>join on=</code> mentions every table in <code>tables=</code>
|}

== Configuration (admins) ==

Common <code>LocalSettings.php</code> / Canasta settings:

<pre>
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultDirection = 'TD';
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultLimit = 500;
$wgSaintapediaGraphMaxLimit = 1000;
$wgSaintapediaGraphClickable = true;
$wgSaintapediaGraphDefaultTheme = 'default';
</pre>

